# A model of equation 4657 that its own realisations cannot rebuild

`Magma.revF34657a` is a model of equation `4657` on `Fin 4`, and its binary clone has
`18` members. Every target settled in the companion files *is* realised in that clone,
so no clone certificate refutes term-definability. What fails is the other half of
term-structurality: the members realising those targets generate only a proper subclone,
and `Magma.revF34657aSub` lists the `2` subclones that contain all of them. `◇` is in none
of the subclones, so none of those members can define `◇` back.

`Magma.revF34657aBad` holds the `2` clone members the subclones miss -- exactly the ones
that do generate `◇`. A target refuted by all of them is therefore not term-structural
from `4657`, over finite magmas and hence over all of them.

This file is generated by `revemit.py`.
-/

